How to deploy directly on your server
--------------------------------------------


Two options are avaliable:
- 1. Use own generated image and deploy it on your server.
- 2. Use the prebuilt image and deploy it on your server.


## 1. Use own generated image and deploy it on your server
-------------------------------------------------
Clone the repository and build the image with the following command:

```bash
./BUILD.sh
```

Then, you can run the image with the following command just to text it:

```bash
./RUN.sh
```

When you are ready to deploy it on your server, you can use the following command:

```bash
.EXPORT.sh
```

The image is generated and saved in the `build` folder. You can copy it to your server and load it with the following command:

```bash
docker load < build/itsme.tar.gz
```

Then, you can run the image on your server with the following command:

```bash
if [ ! -f .env ]; then
  echo ".env file not found. Please create a .env file with the necessary environment variables."
  exit 1
fi
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d
```


## 2. Use the prebuilt image and deploy it on your server
-------------------------------------------------
You can use the prebuilt image `zll/itsme:latest` and deploy it on your server with the following command:
```bash
if [ ! -f .env ]; then
  echo ".env file not found. Please create a .env file with the necessary environment variables."
  exit 1
fi
docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up -d
```